Skip PAA certificates that fail to parse instead of aborting server startup.

The DCL occasionally serves a PAA root certificate that pyca/cryptography's
(Rust) ASN.1 parser rejects (e.g. "error parsing asn1 value: ParseError
{ kind: ExtraData, location: ["Certificate::tbs_cert",
"TbsCertificate::signature_alg"] }"). In 8.1.2, write_paa_root_cert lets that
ValueError propagate through fetch_dcl_certificates (which only catches
ClientError/TimeoutError), so a single malformed cert crashes start() before
the WebSocket server binds :5580 -- taking all Matter devices offline.

Wrap the parse so one bad cert is logged and skipped. Only affects
commissioning of new devices; operating already-commissioned devices does not
need these certs. Remove once fixed upstream.

--- a/matter_server/server/helpers/paa_certificates.py
+++ b/matter_server/server/helpers/paa_certificates.py
@@ -71,7 +71,13 @@
             # via Slack.
             warnings.simplefilter("ignore", CryptographyDeprecationWarning)

-        cert = x509.load_pem_x509_certificate(pem_certificate.encode())
+        try:
+            cert = x509.load_pem_x509_certificate(pem_certificate.encode())
+        except ValueError as err:
+            LOGGER.warning(
+                "Skipping unparseable PAA certificate '%s': %s", subject, err
+            )
+            return False

     ski: x509.SubjectKeyIdentifier = cert.extensions.get_extension_for_class(
         x509.SubjectKeyIdentifier
